course: dictionary
lesson: 7390
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can only tell which meaning the writer means by reading the words around it. The word plunger is a good example. «Pulling back a syringe's plunger makes more room inside» is about a part of a syringe, not a tool for a toilet. The clue is the word syringe.
explain: In the first meaning, a plunger is a tool with a rubber cup on a stick. You push and pull it to clear a blocked sink or toilet. In the second meaning, a plunger is a part that slides in and out of a tube, as in a syringe, a cafetière or a pump. Ask yourself: what is being talked about?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «When you breathe in, the air outside pushes in, just like water into a syringe when you pull the plunger.» Here the plunger is the sliding part of a syringe, because you pull it to draw water in. If your meaning still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: A plunger is a tool with a rubber cup on a stick, used to clear a blocked sink or toilet.
fact: A plunger can also be the part that slides in and out of a tube, such as in a syringe, a cafetière (French press) or a pump.
fact: In a cafetière, the plunger pushes the coffee down.
fact: Pulling back a syringe's plunger makes more room inside, so the pressure drops and the outside air or water is pushed in.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, so always check the words around them to find the right one.
exercise: «The plunger was stuck in the blocked sink, so Dad fetched a new one.» What does plunger mean here? | *A tool with a rubber cup on a stick | A part that slides in and out of a tube | A kind of bird | A cup of coffee
exercise: «Mia pushed the plunger down slowly and the coffee tasted smooth.» What does plunger mean here? | *The part of a cafetière that pushes the coffee down | A type of rubber boot | A tool for a blocked toilet | A glass of water
exercise: «Pulling back the syringe's plunger makes more room inside.» Which word tells you the plunger is not a toilet tool? | *syringe | room | pulling | inside
test: Lily says a plunger is only for toilets. What is the right answer? | Yes, but only in kitchens | No, it is a kind of bird | *No, a plunger can also be a sliding part inside a syringe or pump | Yes, a plunger is only for toilets
test: «When you breathe in, the air outside pushes in, just like water into a syringe when you pull the plunger.» Why is plunger about a syringe here? | Because the sentence is about a toilet | Because it is raining | Because a plunger is a kind of bread | *Because the plunger is the sliding part that is pulled to draw water in
exam: Which meaning of plunger fits «The plunger in the syringe was pulled back slowly»? | *A part that slides in and out of a tube | A rubber cup on a stick | A bird | A glass of water
